{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: recover the unfinished competitive-analytics stages 1–3 from #2220. Queue after the already-promised full I7, Kiro assessment, install clarification, guard timestamps and URL feature delivery. Preserve those priorities and the delivered Stage 0; this request keeps all three remaining outcomes assigned.\n\nThe [published plan](notes/2026-08-31-sentry-agents-dashboard-gap-analysis.md@19eee8f25b0086b0b1c4e39a45598d1878dac69b:15) specifies three implementation stages. #2220 is projected satisfied because receipt #2957/bd9ea4d9 recorded the narrower Stage 0 evidence composition, while #2913 and #2958 explicitly retained later implementation. The original b874 Stage 0 candidate is not an ancestor of main; its documented composition merge443c is. The fixture and plan remain on current main. Do not replay Stage 0 or reinterpret its technical approval as completed analytics.\n\nAt exact main 19eee8f25b0086b0b1c4e39a45598d1878dac69b I loaded and compiled all six actual embedded bundles. [Activity-stats](tailapps/activity-stats/application.sql@19eee8f25b0086b0b1c4e39a45598d1878dac69b:25) exports only event_inventory, request_performance and session_activity and retains five duration buckets. The promised hourly/model/tool tables and enriched panels are absent. The [compiled-schema probe](analytics-compiled-probe.json) and [history/source reconciliation](analytics-recovery-evidence.json) retain this evidence. No later owner of stages1–3 was found in the current request texts/bodies; confirm before duplicating any work.\n\nDeliver the original remaining stages, reconciling current post-I7 source and telemetry evidence:\n1. Add activity_hourly(harness, hour_utc, event_family), where hour_utc is the UTC epoch hour, carrying records, requests, tools, success/failure/unknown outcomes, observed duration total/count, all token families and cost. Replace the five fixed request_performance buckets with about sixteen log-spaced edges from 50ms to five minutes, including the hourly histogram; preserve a separate Codex TTFT histogram. Document P50/P95 interpolation and its actual error bound, zero/unknown/overflow behavior and the writable-schema reset consequence. Keep unrelated bundles unchanged in this stage.\n2. Add model_requests(harness, model, hour_utc) with request and api_error counts, duration histogram, token families, cost and observed/unknown model coverage; and tool_calls(harness, tool_name, hour_utc) with calls, failures, duration histogram, observed input/result-size totals, and Claude tool-decision rejects by source. Raw tool_name is the previously directed bounded aggregate dimension: disclose it clearly in the activity-stats privacy documentation and root catalog, with explicit cardinality/length bounds. Codex model stays unknown unless current documented or scrubbed fixture evidence supports it; do not infer it.\n3. Enrich session_activity with observed main/subagent/auxiliary counts and a bounded distinct agent.name list, API error count and observed duration total, plus the documented session_cost_detail join. Deliver queryable coding-agent panels for permission decisions by source and permission-mode changes over time, MCP health by status/transport/duration/failures per hour with names redacted, observed refusals by model, and cached-input share per hour. Preserve honest guard/gap timeline and completeness/coverage context. Keep the excluded per-session step ledger out of scope.\n\nUse only telemetry already emitted under existing documented gates. No prompts, tool arguments/content, new harness session-store reads or invented vocabularies. Reuse the [scrubbed Stage 0 fixture](tailapps/testdata/claude-code-2.1.251.json@19eee8f25b0086b0b1c4e39a45598d1878dac69b:1); distinguish its observed events from api_refusal and permission_mode_changed, which it did not exercise. Cover documented-but-unobserved inputs with honestly labelled tests and explicit missing coverage, not a claim of captured support. If evidence cannot support a required panel, record the specific gap and preserve its unfulfilled outcome for disposition rather than dropping it.\n\nReconcile the plan to then-current compiler, confinement and accounting contracts; preserve deterministic bounded processing and existing engine limits. Each stage needs fixture-driven column/aggregation/histogram tests that detect omission and query recipes for agent runs, LLM calls, average/P95 duration, model/tool calls/tokens/cost/errors and models/tools/sessions tables. Exercise bucket edges, multiple hours/models/tools, unknown coverage, bounded cardinality and a partial final bucket. State activation/revision/identity consequences accurately; no unjustified RuntimeID change. A reset requirement is documentation and reviewed source only, not permission to reset installed data.\n\nUse request/competitive-analytics-recovery from then-current main. Prefer one final independently reviewed source delivery covering all three stages. If separate stage landings are materially useful, file explicit stage child requests before those implementations and keep an umbrella with all remaining outcomes; do not let one stage receipt silently close the whole recovery again. Publish exact-path primary/companions on current producer bases, obtain fresh Checker Architecture/Security/Simplification review for each delivered exact head, and pass the applicable test/vet/race/demo and module gates at that head. Seal main with full succession, push source/workroom refs, verify CI and remove owned worktrees/branches. All three source outcomes must be delivered or explicitly dispositioned by their responsible requester. No live telemetry reconfiguration, installation, activation, reset, release or service restart is authorized by this request.","body":{"branch":"request/competitive-analytics-recovery","conditions":"Recover all three remaining #2220 analytics stages: hourly/histograms, model/tool tables, session/panels; preserve Stage0/p